Now I have comprehensive data to render a verdict. Let me synthesize all findings.

**Key findings from my independent verification:**

1. **UWM is RSS 2026, not RSS 2025** — factual error persists in key_references
2. **UWM's AdaLN already conditions on BOTH timesteps** (concatenated + projected) — the model already has access to noise-pair information through layer norm modulation
3. **UWM trains in ~40 hours on a single A100** — adapter training is feasible within budget, but proposal's own estimates (300h manual) exceed the 200h constraint
4. **UWM has NOT been evaluated on RoboCasa or LIBERO-PRO** — baselines must be established from scratch
5. **Novelty claim holds up** — no prior work conditions cross-modal attention on the pair of independent noise levels
6. **Register tokens mediate cross-modal exchange** in UWM — DualGate proposal doesn't address how gating interacts with register tokens
7. **Very active concurrent work** — OA-WAM, EA-WM, CKT-WAM, Being-H0.7 all appeared in May 2026, showing extreme competition

