xplicitly.** Describe how DualGate handles the register token attention quadrants. Options: (a) treat registers as belonging to neither modality and leave their attention ungated, (b) apply a separate learned gating for register interactions, or (c) gate registers based on which modality they're attending to.\n\n4. **Narrow the contribution claim** from 'first work to condition cross-modal attention on noise pairs' to something more precise that acknowledges AdaLN's implicit conditioning: e.g., 'first work to apply explicit, learned, per-head attention gating conditioned on independent per-modality noise levels in world action models.'",
